8. Conclusion
The example program is a clear and compact demonstration of KDEPlot. It uses realistic data, relies on sensible defaults and shows how to read the returned points. Adding error handling, formatted or CSV output, and an example with a custom bandwidth would make it a more complete guide for new users and would make it easier to feed the results into a chart.
